# Whitelist deploy. The x:\ESOS folder on disk is a general workspace holding
# dozens of large, untracked sibling projects (Blender scenes, site backups,
# git worktrees, video/data dumps). A denylist kept missing newly-added ones,
# and the upload blew past Vercel's 2 GiB-per-file limit ("File size ... is
# greater than 2 GiB"). So: ignore EVERYTHING by default, then re-include only
# the Eleventy site. This mirrors exactly what the git repo tracks
# (src/, scripts/, and root config files).

# 1. Ignore every top-level entry.
/*

# 2. Re-include only the site.
!/src
!/scripts
!/.eleventy.js
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/vercel.json

# 3. Re-exclude the phantom broken-ACL directory inside src/ — it has corrupt
#    local ACLs that crash the file walker (see commit e6d3846). The live globe
#    files (hero-globe.js, world-mask.png) live directly under src/assets/.
/src/assets/globe
